          "title": "Facing your fears",
          "text": "About one in ten people has a phobia. The most common are fear of spiders, heights and flying. Psychologists treat phobias with 'exposure therapy': slowly, step by step, the patient meets what they're afraid of. Someone who is terrified of spiders first looks at photos, then watches videos, and finally sits near a real spider. 'If you avoided your fear all your life, it would only get stronger,' explains one therapist.",
